---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { withBase } from '../lib/url';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy notice"
  description="Privacy notice (Datenschutzerklärung) for vashisthpatel.com: hosting, cookieless analytics, browser storage and the fintech demo."
  updated="October 2026"
>
  <h1>Privacy notice</h1>
  <p class="lede">Datenschutzerklärung. In short: no cookies, no advertising, no tracking across websites. Fonts, scripts and images are served from this website itself.</p>

  <h2>1. Who is responsible</h2>
  <address>
    Vashisth Patel<br />
    Nerotal 12, 65193 Wiesbaden, Germany<br />
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
  </address>

  <h2>2. Hosting (GitHub Pages)</h2>
  <p>
    This website is hosted on GitHub Pages, a service of GitHub, Inc., 88 Colin P. Kelly Jr. Street, San Francisco,
    CA 94107, USA. When you open a page, your browser sends GitHub technical data that every website receives: your IP
    address, the page requested, the time, and your browser's identification. GitHub uses this to deliver the site and to
    protect it against attacks, and may process it in the USA. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR: a legitimate
    interest in delivering the website securely. See
    <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub's privacy statement</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Visitor statistics (GoatCounter)</h2>
  <p>
    To learn which parts of the site are used, page views and a few named actions (for example which world was opened,
    or which quiz answer was chosen) are counted with
    <a href="https://www.goatcounter.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GoatCounter</a>, operated by
    Martin Tournoij (Ireland), with data stored on servers in Finland and Germany. GoatCounter sets no cookies, stores
    nothing on your device, and does not store your IP address. It records only aggregate figures: the page, the
    referring site, browser and operating system type, screen width, language and the country derived from the IP
    address. To avoid counting one visit twice, a hash of IP address, browser identification and a random value is kept
    in memory for up to eight hours and never written to disk. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR: a legitimate
    interest in understanding how the site is used. You can object at any time (section 7). See
    <a href="https://www.goatcounter.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GoatCounter's privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Settings remembered in your browser</h2>
  <p>
    Some features remember small settings in your own browser, using the browser's session or local storage: whether you
    have seen the Atoms introduction, list or orbit view, whether the arcade is unlocked, your terminal command history,
    your Snake best score and whether game sounds are on. This information stays on your device and is never sent to me
    or anyone else. It is used only to provide the features you use (§ 25(2) no. 2 TDDDG). You can delete it at any time
    in your browser settings.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Fintech demo form</h2>
  <p>
    The <a href={withBase('projects/fintech-qualifier/')}>fintech qualification demo</a> sends the company details you
    enter to an automated workflow (n8n) hosted by Render Services, Inc., USA, where they are analysed to produce the
    score you see. Nothing is sent unless you press submit. Please enter only information about a company, not personal
    data. Submissions are processed only to produce the result and are not stored afterwards.
    The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR: a legitimate interest in providing the demo you asked to run.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Email and links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    If you email me, I use your address and message only to reply. Links to LinkedIn, GitHub, esahubble.org and other
    sites open those sites; their own privacy policies apply once you are there.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the GDPR you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>access the data held about you (Art. 15)</li>
    <li>have it corrected (Art. 16) or deleted (Art. 17)</li>
    <li>restrict its processing (Art. 18) and receive it in a portable format (Art. 20)</li>
    <li>object to processing based on legitimate interests (Art. 21)</li>
    <li>
      complain to a data protection authority (Art. 77), for example
      <a href="https://datenschutz.hessen.de/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Der Hessische Beauftragte für Datenschutz und Informationsfreiheit</a>
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>To use these rights, email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
</LegalLayout>
